      "description": "Developed in collaboration with the police, the emergency services, and driving instructors, the Roadcraft app contains essential learning for emergency responders preparing for the demands of operational driving, and anyone looking to become a better, safer driver.  \n\n\nThe Roadcraft app will help you to\n\n\n• understand and apply the Roadcraft system of car control\n• recognise the human factors that influence your driving and develop strategies to manage them\n• improve your personal risk awareness and competence in handling your vehicle so that you can tackle driving situations safely and effectively\n• apply advanced techniques such as single and multi-stage overtakes, observation links and limit points\n• develop self-assessment skills to continuously improve your driving abilities.\n\n\nThe Roadcraft app is suitable for road users in the UK.  \n\n\n\nWith this app, you get\n\n\n• a digital version of the Roadcraft Handbook, featuring diagrams, self-assessment tasks and video content to support your learning\n• the complete Roadcraft quiz question bank\n• offline access so that you can learn anytime, anywhere\n• updates delivered seamlessly to your device \n\n\nPlease note - this app does not issue certificates. This feature is only available to learners who pass the Roadcraft eLearning course available on the Safe Driving for Life website. \n\n\nPRACTICE AND TEST YOURSELF\n• assess your understanding by practising a total of 130 multiple-choice questions. Got a question wrong? See the correct answer and note the explanation.\n\n\nSEARCH FEATURE\n• want to know more about ‘overtaking’, ‘positioning’, or ‘emergency braking’? Get straight to the content you need with our advanced search tool.\n\n\nENGLISH VOICEOVER\n• if reading is hard for you, like with dyslexia, or if you learn better by listening, use the voiceover feature in the ‘Questions’ section to help you out.\n\n\nPROGRESS GAUGE\n• backed by learning science, use the progress gauge to track your progress.\n\n\nFEEDBACK\n• missing something? Let us know what you’d like to see. We’d love to hear from you with any comments or suggestions about this app.\n\n\nSUPPORT\n• need support? Contact our UK-based team at feedback@williamslea.com or +44 (0)333 202 5070. We listen and respond to your feedback by updating the app and adding new features. So, help others in their studies by letting us know what you’d like to see!",
